    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1136">

                <pb facs="0943" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.001H87/11.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Attorney General</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 14, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith for
                    your information a copy of a communication from Enrique Llorente, expressing
                    apprehension lest General Victoriano Huerta, who it is stated was about to land
                    from the Spanish steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Lopez</hi> at the port of New
                    York, may use the territory of the United States to provoke further armed
                    resistance in Mexico.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
